CURRENT SCOPE

Real-time monitoring of conveyor belt splice condition.
Integration of camera, vibration and load/current sensors.
AI-based multimodal data analysis for early degradation detection.
Generation of Splice Health Index and failure-risk alerts.
Suitable for prototype-scale conveyor belt testing.

FUTURE SCOPE
Integration with industrial-grade sensors for mining environments.
IoT/cloud connectivity for remote monitoring and centralized dashboards.
Advanced AI for Remaining Useful Life (RUL) prediction.
Automatic conveyor speed reduction or shutdown during critical conditions.
Expansion to detect multiple belt damage types across long conveyor systems.

LIMITATIONS
AI performance depends on the quality and quantity of training data.
Dust, vibration and poor lighting can affect sensor/camera accuracy.
Prototype results may differ from real mining-site conditions.
Accurate failure prediction requires long-term operational data.
Industrial deployment requires ruggedized hardware and extensive validation.
